      {
        "id": 4426144087,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOQ6ulRs8AAAABB9GZVw",
        "number": 280,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "Support running Agent.loop in lockstep with consumer of Agent.run",
        "body": "Add a buffer argument to Agent.run that controls the buffer size.  The\ndefault, `None`, maintains the current behavior of fully decoupling\nthem. At `buffer=0`, they will run in lockstep.\n\nThe reason I want this is so that a custom loop and client code that\ndo out-of-band messaging will interact in a predictable way.\n\n(In particular, when doing a durable agent loop, I want to be able to\nsend all the streaming messages from the client code, but the messages\nneed to be queued *before* a new llm call is made.)\n",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai-python/pull/280",
        "created_at": "2026-09-02T19:58:02Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-09-04T21:22:08Z",
        "closed_at": "2026-09-04T21:22:07Z",
        "merged_at": "2026-09-04T21:22:07Z",
        "merge_commit_sha": "22896783337d728f7c6d90cb049a8f2a39209295",
        "draft": false,
        "user": {
          "id": 340349,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDM0OQ==",
          "login": "msullivan",
          "type": "User",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/msullivan"
        },
        "head": {
          "sha": "1ab4322d52f14f1c8aa4bc03fc37a63ad0cc2c38",
          "ref": "lockstep-2"
        },
        "base": {
          "sha": "14930fba59a6c5f3f27816bf26844b4ca288cff4",
          "ref": "main"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": 4437493655,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOQ6ulRs8AAAABCH7Hlw",
        "number": 285,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "Support anthropic>=1.0.0 and openai>=3.0.0 (httpx2 change)",
        "body": "Stop doing our own runtime enforcement of the client objects for anthropic and openai, just pass them through and see what they allow. (anthropic will only allow httpx2, openai has compat goo to allow both.)\r\n\r\nBump the minimum version of openai to 2.34.0, because it turned out that was already the case.\r\n\r\nAdd CI to test different upstream SDK versions.\r\n(Though it is still all a bit marginal because we don't actually make any requests in CI!)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai-python/pull/285",
        "created_at": "2026-09-03T22:30:31Z",
