        "number": 260,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "fix(types): detect video media types in FilePart.from_bytes",
        "body": "## What\n\n`FilePart.from_bytes()` could not detect video files: it only checked image and audio signatures, so `file_part(video_bytes)` raised `ValueError` unless you passed `media_type` manually. The `VIDEO_SIGNATURES` table already existed but had no public wrapper.\n\n## Why\n\nImage and audio detection work; video doesn't — a concrete capability gap for attaching video input (e.g. video-capable gateway models) and video round-trips. `ai.file_part(open(\"clip.mp4\", \"rb\").read())` should just work.\n\n## How\n\n- Add `media.detect_video_media_type()` mirroring the existing image/audio wrappers\n- Chain it into `FilePart.from_bytes`: image → audio → video\n\n## Tests\n\n- `detect_video_media_type`: mp4 detection, base64 input, rejects non-video (image)\n- `FilePart.from_bytes`: video/mp4 detection\n\nFull local gate green: ruff format/check, mypy, ty, 690 pytest tests, check-examples.\n\n## Known limitation (pre-existing, not changed)\n\nWebm is container-ambiguous — `audio/webm` is checked before `video/webm`, so webm video still reports `audio/webm`. Reordering would regress genuine webm audio detection. Also note `video/quicktime` is shadowed by the mp4 signature's wildcard size byte — both pre-existing table behavior.",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai-python/pull/260",
        "created_at": "2026-08-08T07:43:00Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-08-18T07:16:48Z",
        "closed_at": "2026-08-18T07:16:48Z",
        "merged_at": "2026-08-18T07:16:48Z",
        "merge_commit_sha": "89fa2f3db2d4bf080c657999e8793cf6934d58e1",
        "draft": false,
        "user": {
          "id": 146335736,
          "node_id": "U_kgDOCLjn-A",
          "login": "jaygupta17",
          "type": "User",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/jaygupta17"
        },
        "head": {
          "sha": "ba6989e1e7c671f2df560bb5e8b7633460b2ca01",
          "ref": "fix/file-part-video-detection"
        },
        "base": {
          "sha": "1d7220a73b094c2680404cc39f679f442032d58c",
          "ref": "main"
        }
