      {
        "id": 4084861843,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOQ6ulRs7zeguT",
        "number": 225,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "Add Google provider with generateContent protocol",
        "body": "Adds a Google Gemini provider following the Anthropic provider's pattern: the official `google-genai` SDK handles transport, and the protocol layer does the message/params translation.\n\n- `GoogleProvider` (handles `google` / `@ai-sdk/google`) with a lazily-created `genai.Client`, `GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY`/`GEMINI_API_KEY`/`GOOGLE_API_KEY` env fallbacks, `list_models()`, and `probe()`. `google-genai>=2.0.0` ships as the `ai[google]` extra.\n- `GoogleGenerateContentProtocol` streams via `generate_content_stream`, mapping text/thought parts, function calls, code-execution parts, inline data, and usage into framework events. `thought_signature` round-trips through provider metadata so multi-turn function calling works with thinking models.\n- Finish reasons are normalized to the OTel vocabulary on `StreamEnd`, along with `response_id`/`response_model`; unmapped raw values land in provider metadata.\n- Reasoning effort maps to `thinking_level` on Gemini 3 (`None` → `minimal`, which rejects a zero budget) and to a token budget on earlier models, which reject `thinking_level`.\n- Built-in tool factories: `google_search`, `url_context`, `code_execution`.\n- Transport errors are mapped into the provider error hierarchy (the SDK doesn't wrap httpx errors), and safety-blocked prompts raise instead of yielding an empty message.\n\nKnown limitations, to be addressed in follow-ups: grounding metadata (search queries/citations) for `google_search`/`url_context` is not surfaced as builtin tool events, explicit `cached_content` doesn't strip conflicting system/tools fields, and Vertex AI is not supported yet.\n\nVerified against the live Gemini API: text, tool-call round-trip, structured output, thinking on 2.5/3, and error mapping.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai-python/pull/225",
        "created_at": "2026-07-19T05:30:43Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-08-17T18:25:49Z",
        "closed_at": "2026-08-17T18:25:48Z",
